1
00:00:38,383 --> 00:00:39,383
How are you?

2
00:00:47,103 --> 00:00:48,183
Are you okay?

3
00:00:51,983 --> 00:00:53,663
If you don't say anything,
I'm coming in.

4
00:01:27,223 --> 00:01:29,223
I've been with Dee since I was 17.

5
00:01:30,623 --> 00:01:34,263
He's jealous and possessive.

6
00:01:36,303 --> 00:01:37,903
He doesn't like me going out.

7
00:01:41,823 --> 00:01:43,663
I thought it was sweet
when I was young.

8
00:01:47,143 --> 00:01:48,743
So I went along
with everything he wanted.

9
00:01:52,903 --> 00:01:55,463
Later, when he became a triad boss,

10
00:01:57,663 --> 00:01:59,863
he would take all the frustration
he felt outside...

11
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,383
out on me.

12
00:02:05,343 --> 00:02:07,223
Because I'm Dee's woman,

13
00:02:07,903 --> 00:02:09,503
no one dared to help me.

14
00:02:11,543 --> 00:02:13,583
I even thought about ending it all.

15
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:18,983
Luckily, I met Ben.

16
00:02:21,103 --> 00:02:24,703
He was the only one willing
to listen and comfort me.

17
00:02:25,743 --> 00:02:27,423
Even though it started
as a transaction,

18
00:02:31,103 --> 00:02:33,903
he made me feel...

19
00:02:36,623 --> 00:02:38,463
that in this world,

20
00:02:42,543 --> 00:02:44,343
there's still someone
who cares about me.

21
00:02:50,023 --> 00:02:53,503
I've always thought
that he liked me.

22
00:02:56,023 --> 00:02:57,023
And sure enough,

23
00:02:59,063 --> 00:03:00,703
he risked his life to save me.

24
00:03:03,663 --> 00:03:05,103
Do you know
that by coming to save you,

25
00:03:05,183 --> 00:03:06,183
the consequences are very serious?

26
00:03:08,143 --> 00:03:10,703
If the police catch him,
he'll go straight to prison.

27
00:03:11,703 --> 00:03:14,903
If Dee finds him, he's a dead man.

28
00:03:16,023 --> 00:03:17,063
I know.

29
00:03:17,983 --> 00:03:19,743
I didn't want to accuse him of rape.

30
00:03:19,823 --> 00:03:21,303
But Dee forced me to.

31
00:03:21,383 --> 00:03:23,663
If I didn't, he was going
to beat Ben to death.

32
00:03:24,343 --> 00:03:25,543
I'm begging you.

33
00:03:26,343 --> 00:03:28,543
Please help him.

34
00:03:30,303 --> 00:03:33,423
Good deeds are rewarded.
Please help him.

35
00:05:06,703 --> 00:05:09,463
(Episode 8)

36
00:05:09,463 --> 00:05:10,863
(This is a work of fiction.)

37
00:05:21,663 --> 00:05:22,663
Get up.

38
00:05:29,463 --> 00:05:30,623
What's going on?

39
00:05:32,903 --> 00:05:33,903
Fatty,

40
00:05:34,663 --> 00:05:35,743
where's your friend?

41
00:05:37,663 --> 00:05:39,103
Do you know who my father is?

42
00:05:42,183 --> 00:05:43,183
I know.

43
00:05:43,623 --> 00:05:45,263
Just a has-been gangster.

44
00:05:45,703 --> 00:05:47,223
Dee sent me here to find someone.

45
00:05:47,543 --> 00:05:49,263
Last chance. Where is he?

46
00:05:52,903 --> 00:05:53,903
I'm telling you,

47
00:05:54,503 --> 00:05:56,903
if you touch me,
you'll be in big trouble.

48
00:05:57,463 --> 00:05:59,063
I love trouble.

49
00:05:59,623 --> 00:06:00,623
Trouble.

50
00:06:27,903 --> 00:06:30,543
Come on, tell me where he is,

51
00:06:30,863 --> 00:06:33,063
and I'll let you keep
those fat fingers.

52
00:06:39,823 --> 00:06:41,143
Save your breath.

53
00:06:42,023 --> 00:06:43,223
You look so cool.

54
00:06:46,023 --> 00:06:47,023
I wonder.

55
00:06:48,383 --> 00:06:49,503
If you lose a few fingers,

56
00:06:50,063 --> 00:06:51,463
will you look like Doraemon?

57
00:07:14,703 --> 00:07:15,703
Thank you.

58
00:07:28,023 --> 00:07:29,023
Excuse me.

59
00:07:30,943 --> 00:07:33,383
I've applied to be
the administrator of her estate.

60
00:07:33,463 --> 00:07:34,543
I have also filed an application...

61
00:07:34,623 --> 00:07:36,503
to object to you
being the administrator.

62
00:07:37,783 --> 00:07:39,223
You have no right
to handle the body by force.

63
00:07:39,383 --> 00:07:40,743
I've applied for an injunction.

64
00:07:40,823 --> 00:07:42,263
You'll receive the summons soon.

65
00:07:43,943 --> 00:07:45,143
I am Ma Sze Ming's father.

66
00:07:45,583 --> 00:07:46,823
I'm here to claim the body.

67
00:07:47,143 --> 00:07:48,743
I am Ma Sze Ming's wife.

68
00:07:49,023 --> 00:07:50,663
The body should be claimed by me.

69
00:07:51,463 --> 00:07:54,343
In a 2021 judicial review case,

70
00:07:54,583 --> 00:07:56,863
the government reached
a consensus with the applicant.

71
00:07:57,023 --> 00:08:00,383
The FEHD has no policy
or internal guidelines...

72
00:08:00,463 --> 00:08:03,503
to prevent or restrict in any way...

73
00:08:03,583 --> 00:08:05,903
same-sex spouses from handling
the deceased's funeral arrangements.

74
00:08:06,343 --> 00:08:08,223
A same-sex spouse married abroad...

75
00:08:08,303 --> 00:08:11,143
also has the right
to claim the body.

76
00:08:11,863 --> 00:08:13,863
We have formally applied
for an injunction.

77
00:08:14,023 --> 00:08:16,103
If you prioritize the parents...

78
00:08:16,183 --> 00:08:17,943
and let them claim the body
before the court rules,

79
00:08:18,023 --> 00:08:19,863
all of you could be held liable.

80
00:08:21,223 --> 00:08:22,863
Why don't you discuss it further...

81
00:08:22,943 --> 00:08:24,543
and claim it
once you have a consensus?

82
00:08:25,183 --> 00:08:27,023
I'm her biological father.
I have priority.

83
00:08:27,103 --> 00:08:28,103
I want to claim it now.

84
00:08:28,223 --> 00:08:30,343
If you let someone claim it
without verifying their rights,

85
00:08:30,343 --> 00:08:31,343
that is negligence.

86
00:08:31,343 --> 00:08:32,863
I'll file a complaint
and make you lose your job.

87
00:08:32,943 --> 00:08:34,303
If you don't let me claim it now,

88
00:08:34,383 --> 00:08:35,903
I'll also file a complaint
and make you lose your job.

89
00:08:38,383 --> 00:08:40,183
I'm losing my job either way.

90
00:08:40,383 --> 00:08:41,623
I'm going to take a break then.

91
00:08:41,703 --> 00:08:43,503
Complain all you want.

92
00:08:49,223 --> 00:08:51,303
This is my family matter.
What's it to you?

93
00:08:51,383 --> 00:08:53,103
Why are you getting in the way here?

94
00:08:53,863 --> 00:08:55,863
I've been your daughter's
best friend since childhood.

95
00:08:58,503 --> 00:09:00,263
You didn't know she got married.

96
00:09:00,463 --> 00:09:02,543
You didn't know we've been friends
for 20 years either.

97
00:09:02,823 --> 00:09:03,823
Now that she's gone,

98
00:09:03,823 --> 00:09:05,303
you rush out
and say you're her father.

99
00:09:05,383 --> 00:09:06,863
You want to control everything.

100
00:09:07,223 --> 00:09:08,383
Have you no shame?

101
00:09:12,583 --> 00:09:13,583
Don't be so smug.

102
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:16,303
You're bound to lose
in court anyway.

103
00:09:28,337 --> 00:09:29,337
Thank you for helping me.

104
00:09:29,977 --> 00:09:30,977
It's the least I could do.

105
00:09:31,977 --> 00:09:33,977
Sze Ming helped us a lot before.

106
00:09:34,697 --> 00:09:36,177
So do I just wait
for the court date now?

107
00:09:36,257 --> 00:09:38,457
Can I take her away
after the judge's ruling?

108
00:09:50,977 --> 00:09:53,057
Actually, the chances
of winning this case aren't high.

109
00:09:54,257 --> 00:09:56,297
I was just bluffing earlier
to buy us some time.

110
00:09:57,937 --> 00:10:00,057
Aside from a 2021 case
where the government...

111
00:10:00,257 --> 00:10:02,457
reached a consensus
with a judicial review applicant...

112
00:10:03,057 --> 00:10:04,297
to allow same-sex spouses...

113
00:10:04,377 --> 00:10:06,417
to handle
the deceased's funeral affairs,

114
00:10:07,417 --> 00:10:10,497
the law basically hasn't changed.

115
00:10:11,537 --> 00:10:12,937
It's lagging behind in many ways.

116
00:10:14,297 --> 00:10:16,657
Regarding same-sex spouses
and parents...

117
00:10:16,737 --> 00:10:18,977
fighting to be
the estate administrator,

118
00:10:19,777 --> 00:10:21,177
there's no precedent in Hong Kong.

119
00:10:21,897 --> 00:10:24,057
No one has ever successfully...

120
00:10:24,137 --> 00:10:25,657
applied for an injunction...

121
00:10:25,737 --> 00:10:28,017
to stop parents
from handling the deceased's body.

122
00:10:31,977 --> 00:10:34,417
Did she leave
any concrete evidence...

123
00:10:34,937 --> 00:10:36,457
proving she wanted
to stay in Australia?

124
00:10:38,017 --> 00:10:41,057
Recordings, emails, or texts.

125
00:10:41,337 --> 00:10:42,377
Anything like that would work.

126
00:10:55,857 --> 00:10:57,217
This is our proof.

127
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:05,137
This really was her wish.

128
00:11:06,417 --> 00:11:07,737
It was always her dream...

129
00:11:07,817 --> 00:11:09,297
to buy a big farm over there...

130
00:11:10,097 --> 00:11:11,697
and live a self-sufficient life.

131
00:11:13,937 --> 00:11:15,777
But she wanted to earn more money
in Hong Kong first.

132
00:11:16,777 --> 00:11:17,977
So I waited for her in Australia.

133
00:11:19,977 --> 00:11:20,977
I understand.

134
00:11:23,017 --> 00:11:24,897
But the court relies on evidence.

135
00:11:26,657 --> 00:11:28,657
It would be best if she left a will,

136
00:11:29,057 --> 00:11:31,577
stating in writing that she wanted
to be buried in Australia.

137
00:11:33,017 --> 00:11:34,257
We're so young.

138
00:11:35,017 --> 00:11:36,617
Who would think of
making a will so early?

139
00:11:40,297 --> 00:11:41,297
And...

140
00:11:42,377 --> 00:11:43,937
I never thought
she would leave so suddenly.

141
00:11:55,457 --> 00:11:56,777
If I were a man,

142
00:11:58,977 --> 00:12:00,857
would I be able
to claim her body now?

143
00:12:14,537 --> 00:12:16,577
No matter how difficult
this case is,

144
00:12:17,777 --> 00:12:19,177
I'll fight to the very end.

145
00:12:21,457 --> 00:12:22,857
This is my promise to her.

146
00:12:28,137 --> 00:12:29,537
I'll definitely do my best
to help you.

147
00:12:51,617 --> 00:12:52,617
Yes!

148
00:12:53,137 --> 00:12:54,137
Yes!

149
00:12:54,897 --> 00:12:55,897
I can truly feel...

150
00:12:55,897 --> 00:12:57,657
the love between Cathy and Sze Ming.

151
00:12:58,377 --> 00:13:00,777
I really hope they can go back
to Australia together.

152
00:13:01,897 --> 00:13:03,257
I don't think she has much money.

153
00:13:03,337 --> 00:13:04,897
You'll help her
until the end, right?

154
00:13:05,577 --> 00:13:07,817
Of course. I love helping people.

155
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:10,697
Find out more about Counselor Ma.

156
00:13:11,897 --> 00:13:13,777
I know you're not
at Senior's level yet.

157
00:13:14,137 --> 00:13:15,137
But just do your best.

158
00:13:16,177 --> 00:13:17,257
Try to feel him out.

159
00:13:18,057 --> 00:13:19,457
See if he's willing to settle.

160
00:13:20,057 --> 00:13:21,057
Okay.

161
00:13:24,617 --> 00:13:26,537
- Hello?
- Has Ben contacted you?

162
00:13:26,817 --> 00:13:27,817
No, why?

163
00:13:28,097 --> 00:13:29,817
He promised to call me today.

164
00:13:29,977 --> 00:13:31,897
But he hasn't yet,
and I can't reach him.

165
00:13:31,977 --> 00:13:33,097
I'm worried.

166
00:13:33,617 --> 00:13:35,137
I'll find him. Wait for my call.

167
00:14:11,937 --> 00:14:12,937
Hello?

168
00:14:14,657 --> 00:14:15,977
I know where your woman is.

169
00:14:16,817 --> 00:14:18,297
As long as you hand them over.

170
00:14:22,737 --> 00:14:24,817
Fine. See you later.

171
00:14:29,377 --> 00:14:30,457
Did you find Ben?

172
00:14:33,537 --> 00:14:34,697
He's with Dee.

173
00:14:41,177 --> 00:14:42,377
Are you going to trade me for him?

174
00:14:44,297 --> 00:14:45,657
Stay in the car later.

175
00:14:46,537 --> 00:14:48,057
Don't come out
no matter what they say.

176
00:14:49,057 --> 00:14:51,977
Trust me if you want to save Ben.

177
00:14:52,617 --> 00:14:53,897
You won't have
to go back to Dee either.

178
00:14:53,977 --> 00:14:54,977
Understand?

179
00:15:06,097 --> 00:15:07,097
Where's my woman?

180
00:15:12,417 --> 00:15:13,417
Tell her to come in.

181
00:15:13,977 --> 00:15:16,177
Turn on the AC first. It's hot.

182
00:15:21,417 --> 00:15:22,417
Where are they?

183
00:15:35,377 --> 00:15:36,497
Do me a favor.

184
00:15:38,057 --> 00:15:40,217
Let them go,
and let your woman go too.

185
00:15:52,057 --> 00:15:53,577
I have plenty of money.

186
00:15:54,417 --> 00:15:55,937
Right now, I'm losing face.

187
00:15:56,177 --> 00:15:57,377
My pride!

188
00:15:58,217 --> 00:15:59,657
If you force your woman
to go to court,

189
00:16:01,377 --> 00:16:02,497
and I'm the defense lawyer,

190
00:16:02,937 --> 00:16:04,097
think about how much trouble
you'll be in.

191
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:06,857
I've handled so many cases for you.

192
00:16:07,097 --> 00:16:08,177
I know all your secrets.

193
00:16:08,457 --> 00:16:09,457
Are you threatening me?

194
00:16:09,977 --> 00:16:11,057
I'll take you down with me.

195
00:16:12,017 --> 00:16:13,297
If you think...

196
00:16:13,737 --> 00:16:16,297
another lawyer can beat me in court,

197
00:16:17,697 --> 00:16:19,177
you wouldn't let me
overcharge you...

198
00:16:19,257 --> 00:16:20,257
and keep coming back to me.

199
00:16:20,817 --> 00:16:22,217
I'm a major client of yours!

200
00:16:22,537 --> 00:16:24,777
You would offend me over a gigolo?

201
00:16:25,577 --> 00:16:28,617
You're my client,
but I'm your savior.

202
00:16:28,817 --> 00:16:31,817
If not for me, you would be
in Stanley Prison, Dee.

203
00:16:33,537 --> 00:16:35,017
I hate it when people threaten me.

204
00:16:35,097 --> 00:16:36,097
You're being so arrogant.

205
00:16:36,137 --> 00:16:37,977
I won't let them go.
I'll take you too!

206
00:16:39,737 --> 00:16:41,337
You enjoy threatening me, don't you?

207
00:16:41,537 --> 00:16:43,097
I'll chop off his hands!

208
00:16:43,337 --> 00:16:44,337
Wait.

209
00:17:00,257 --> 00:17:01,977
Does he have magic hands?

210
00:17:02,657 --> 00:17:03,857
Why are you so protective of him?

211
00:17:06,097 --> 00:17:07,737
Always threatening
to chop off limbs.

212
00:17:08,577 --> 00:17:09,697
That's so old-fashioned.

213
00:17:10,817 --> 00:17:12,857
Have some water and calm down.

214
00:17:13,257 --> 00:17:14,257
Let's talk this through.

215
00:17:17,657 --> 00:17:19,297
Fine, let's see what you're up to.

216
00:18:24,497 --> 00:18:25,497
Hey.

217
00:18:27,297 --> 00:18:28,297
Hey.

218
00:18:32,257 --> 00:18:33,417
Don't do anything stupid.

219
00:18:34,817 --> 00:18:35,897
I know that your goods...

220
00:18:36,177 --> 00:18:38,417
are at the Yuen Long laundromat,
disguised as laundry detergent.

221
00:18:40,257 --> 00:18:41,297
I've scheduled an email...

222
00:18:41,377 --> 00:18:43,017
to be sent to the police
in 15 minutes.

223
00:18:44,497 --> 00:18:46,177
If any one of us doesn't leave,

224
00:18:46,897 --> 00:18:48,417
I won't be able
to cancel that email.

225
00:18:52,777 --> 00:18:55,137
Time flies when you're having fun.

226
00:18:55,657 --> 00:18:56,937
You only have five minutes left.

227
00:19:01,737 --> 00:19:02,737
Let them go.

228
00:19:07,257 --> 00:19:08,817
I said, let them go!

229
00:19:51,250 --> 00:19:52,850
I didn't expect you
to be such a good fighter.

230
00:19:53,290 --> 00:19:55,570
My apologies.

231
00:19:56,810 --> 00:19:59,050
Dee is a madman.
He'll definitely retaliate.

232
00:19:59,930 --> 00:20:00,930
Take good care of her.

233
00:20:02,930 --> 00:20:06,370
I'm leaving Hong Kong.
I can't keep involving you guys.

234
00:20:07,090 --> 00:20:10,170
Right, hurry up.
Better leave tonight.

235
00:20:14,650 --> 00:20:16,250
Is there somewhere
I can sleep for a bit?

236
00:20:16,330 --> 00:20:17,370
What?

237
00:20:17,370 --> 00:20:18,370
Fighting is exhausting.

238
00:20:20,250 --> 00:20:21,250
Go to my room.

239
00:20:22,810 --> 00:20:23,810
Follow me.

240
00:20:40,050 --> 00:20:41,050
It's cold over there.

241
00:20:42,170 --> 00:20:43,250
I brought a jacket for you.

242
00:20:57,530 --> 00:20:59,010
Why don't you come with me?

243
00:21:05,170 --> 00:21:07,370
My services are limited
to Hong Kong.

244
00:21:09,010 --> 00:21:10,290
You helped me so much.

245
00:21:12,210 --> 00:21:13,770
I really thought you liked me.

246
00:21:14,890 --> 00:21:16,010
I do like you.

247
00:21:17,490 --> 00:21:18,730
But not in that way.

248
00:21:20,690 --> 00:21:23,490
I truly want you to be happy
and have a good life.

249
00:21:27,650 --> 00:21:28,650
Okay.

250
00:21:29,770 --> 00:21:30,850
Bye.

251
00:21:32,650 --> 00:21:33,650
Should I walk you to a taxi?

252
00:21:35,130 --> 00:21:36,130
No need.

253
00:21:38,530 --> 00:21:39,530
Stay with her.

254
00:22:17,410 --> 00:22:18,410
You're awake?

255
00:22:19,570 --> 00:22:20,570
How are you?

256
00:22:22,530 --> 00:22:23,530
I'm fine.

257
00:22:24,890 --> 00:22:26,090
Did anyone get hurt just now?

258
00:22:26,930 --> 00:22:28,730
Yes, Dee's gang.

259
00:22:29,570 --> 00:22:31,130
You were like Superwoman just now.

260
00:22:31,210 --> 00:22:32,290
You fought 10 of them by yourself.

261
00:22:32,610 --> 00:22:33,730
You saved all of us.

262
00:22:36,970 --> 00:22:38,730
But what happened just now?

263
00:22:38,810 --> 00:22:40,890
How did you suddenly become
such a good fighter?

264
00:22:42,530 --> 00:22:45,210
I asked a ghost who is
a good fighter to possess me.

265
00:22:47,770 --> 00:22:48,770
So what?

266
00:22:48,930 --> 00:22:50,410
I'm going to negotiate
with Dee later.

267
00:22:50,650 --> 00:22:51,730
I want you to be my backup.

268
00:22:52,250 --> 00:22:53,810
How? I'm already dead.

269
00:22:54,210 --> 00:22:55,410
If he tries anything funny,

270
00:22:55,490 --> 00:22:57,050
I'll give you a signal
to possess me.

271
00:22:57,730 --> 00:22:58,730
What's the signal?

272
00:22:59,130 --> 00:23:00,330
Drinking ice water.

273
00:23:02,730 --> 00:23:03,810
So that's how it works.

274
00:23:04,130 --> 00:23:05,530
Then if you want any skills
in the future,

275
00:23:05,610 --> 00:23:06,850
you can just call
for a ghost possession.

276
00:23:07,970 --> 00:23:09,970
Only if the ghost is reliable.

277
00:23:10,610 --> 00:23:12,890
If the possession lasts too long,
you'll be in danger.

278
00:23:13,130 --> 00:23:14,250
The ghost will be in danger too.

279
00:23:15,490 --> 00:23:17,250
So during the whole fight just now,

280
00:23:17,330 --> 00:23:19,090
you didn't remember
or feel anything?

281
00:23:25,130 --> 00:23:26,130
Hello?

282
00:23:26,130 --> 00:23:28,850
Master, Counselor Ma
refuses to settle.

283
00:23:30,250 --> 00:23:32,450
Okay, that's to be expected.

284
00:23:36,730 --> 00:23:38,210
Can you drive me back to the office?

285
00:24:10,930 --> 00:24:13,370
It's rare to see you
so worried about a case.

286
00:24:17,970 --> 00:24:19,050
It's not looking good.

287
00:24:19,890 --> 00:24:21,450
But I'm confident I can handle it.

288
00:24:22,890 --> 00:24:24,090
Is there anything I can do to help?

289
00:24:30,330 --> 00:24:32,010
Do you think the people
in your car group...

290
00:24:32,090 --> 00:24:33,770
might know something about him?

291
00:24:34,530 --> 00:24:36,770
Alan's father has
a triad background.

292
00:24:37,090 --> 00:24:38,610
He should know people
on both sides of the law.

293
00:24:39,290 --> 00:24:40,530
I'll ask him to find out for you.

294
00:24:48,770 --> 00:24:50,930
I really can give you the money
to open a restaurant.

295
00:24:51,690 --> 00:24:53,010
I told you, that's just my hobby.

296
00:25:01,930 --> 00:25:03,810
Maybe it's because
I've always blamed myself.

297
00:25:04,490 --> 00:25:06,330
I wasn't attentive enough
to my mom then.

298
00:25:08,650 --> 00:25:11,450
Or subconsciously,
I feel that by helping others,

299
00:25:12,770 --> 00:25:14,610
I hope they won't end up
like my mom.

300
00:25:16,530 --> 00:25:17,930
In a way, I suppose
I'm making amends.

301
00:25:22,930 --> 00:25:24,770
What's wrong? Are you touched?

302
00:25:26,730 --> 00:25:28,210
You're a fool.

303
00:25:28,210 --> 00:25:29,450
Those are
completely different things.

304
00:25:31,490 --> 00:25:33,370
I guess fortune favors fools.

305
00:25:33,770 --> 00:25:35,890
If I weren't in this line of work,
how would I have met you?

306
00:25:40,130 --> 00:25:41,410
The deceased, Ma Sze Ming,

307
00:25:41,490 --> 00:25:44,570
had not lived with her parents
for nearly 20 years.

308
00:25:45,490 --> 00:25:48,890
They were estranged
and rarely saw each other.

309
00:25:50,490 --> 00:25:52,690
My client, Ms. Man Cho Ying,

310
00:25:53,130 --> 00:25:56,330
was legally married to the deceased
in Australia for over five years.

311
00:25:57,370 --> 00:26:00,050
The deceased also bought a house
in Australia before she died,

312
00:26:00,130 --> 00:26:02,290
planning to settle down there
with my client.

313
00:26:02,610 --> 00:26:04,330
She even left a card...

314
00:26:04,410 --> 00:26:07,490
clearly stating her wish
to be with my client...

315
00:26:07,570 --> 00:26:10,050
and live in Australia forever.

316
00:26:12,450 --> 00:26:13,970
In a previous case,

317
00:26:14,690 --> 00:26:18,330
the government reached a consensus
with the judicial review applicant.

318
00:26:18,890 --> 00:26:21,690
Same-sex spouses
can inherit estates,

319
00:26:21,770 --> 00:26:24,490
with rights equal
to opposite-sex spouses.

320
00:26:25,730 --> 00:26:26,730
Therefore,

321
00:26:26,730 --> 00:26:29,610
we apply to revoke the defendant,
Mr. Ma Kwan Ho,

322
00:26:29,690 --> 00:26:31,210
as the administrator of the estate.

323
00:26:31,570 --> 00:26:33,290
The hearing is
on the 12th of next month.

324
00:26:33,890 --> 00:26:37,090
I hope the court
respects the deceased's wishes...

325
00:26:37,490 --> 00:26:38,930
and issues
an interim injunction first,

326
00:26:39,010 --> 00:26:42,050
preventing Mr. Ma Kwan Ho
from claiming the body,

327
00:26:42,610 --> 00:26:45,330
to fulfill the deceased's wish
to be buried in Australia.

328
00:26:46,570 --> 00:26:48,010
That concludes my submission.

329
00:26:53,130 --> 00:26:54,130
Mr. Ma.

330
00:27:03,930 --> 00:27:04,930
Your Honor.

331
00:27:08,450 --> 00:27:11,610
Hong Kong law does not
recognize same-sex marriage.

332
00:27:13,610 --> 00:27:16,490
Furthermore, the so-called wishes
of the deceased...

333
00:27:17,450 --> 00:27:19,090
consist only of a property deed...

334
00:27:19,170 --> 00:27:21,170
and a two-line handwritten card.

335
00:27:22,090 --> 00:27:25,130
There is no formal will...

336
00:27:25,530 --> 00:27:26,930
or any other substantial evidence.

337
00:27:30,570 --> 00:27:33,730
Chinese people value the concept
of returning to one's roots.

338
00:27:34,570 --> 00:27:36,170
One must return home after death.

339
00:27:37,130 --> 00:27:38,130
Therefore, I believe...

340
00:27:38,210 --> 00:27:40,650
I am the most appropriate person...

341
00:27:40,730 --> 00:27:42,130
to handle my daughter's funeral.

342
00:27:44,850 --> 00:27:45,850
Besides,

343
00:27:46,410 --> 00:27:49,690
the plaintiff claims I was estranged
from the deceased.

344
00:27:50,690 --> 00:27:52,490
This is absolutely illogical.

345
00:27:53,370 --> 00:27:55,930
If we were truly that estranged,

346
00:27:56,250 --> 00:27:58,890
how could I have known
about my daughter's passing...

347
00:27:58,970 --> 00:28:00,730
even earlier than the plaintiff?

348
00:28:00,930 --> 00:28:02,730
And how could I have
successfully applied...

349
00:28:03,050 --> 00:28:05,490
to be the administrator
of my daughter's estate?

350
00:28:09,610 --> 00:28:10,610
Your Honor,

351
00:28:12,690 --> 00:28:14,330
my daughter's passing...

352
00:28:15,610 --> 00:28:17,930
is already a painful blow to us.

353
00:28:20,210 --> 00:28:21,210
To be in court today,

354
00:28:22,610 --> 00:28:25,330
and having to fight for my rights
as her biological father,

355
00:28:25,410 --> 00:28:26,410
I think...

356
00:28:30,170 --> 00:28:31,170
it's ridiculous.

357
00:28:33,010 --> 00:28:34,810
This shouldn't have happened.

358
00:28:37,290 --> 00:28:38,450
That is all for my submission.

359
00:28:44,530 --> 00:28:45,890
Handling the body...

360
00:28:45,890 --> 00:28:48,130
is the responsibility
of the estate administrator.

361
00:28:49,090 --> 00:28:52,770
As Hong Kong law does not
recognize same-sex marriage,

362
00:28:53,650 --> 00:28:55,370
and the deceased has no children,

363
00:28:56,010 --> 00:28:57,490
the defendant, Ma Kwan Ho,

364
00:28:57,490 --> 00:28:59,810
as the father
of the deceased, Ma Sze Ming,

365
00:29:00,690 --> 00:29:03,570
appears to have priority
to be the estate administrator.

366
00:29:04,810 --> 00:29:07,490
This court sees no clear evidence...

367
00:29:07,810 --> 00:29:10,170
that the deceased's wishes
overturn this principle.

368
00:29:11,530 --> 00:29:13,450
Therefore, the defendant,
Ma Kwan Ho,

369
00:29:13,970 --> 00:29:16,490
is the most suitable person
to handle the body.

370
00:29:18,090 --> 00:29:21,010
Therefore, I hereby rule...

371
00:29:21,930 --> 00:29:24,130
against the plaintiff, Man Cho Ying.

372
00:29:26,330 --> 00:29:29,570
The defendant, Ma Kwan Ho,
is the legal estate administrator.

373
00:29:30,450 --> 00:29:33,610
The plaintiff shall bear
the defendant's legal costs.

374
00:29:34,930 --> 00:29:35,930
Court is adjourned.

375
00:29:36,170 --> 00:29:37,170
Court.

376
00:29:42,210 --> 00:29:44,610
I wonder how much longer we will
have to wait. It's about to rain.

377
00:29:47,050 --> 00:29:48,930
- Mr. Ma.
- Mr. Ma.

378
00:29:49,090 --> 00:29:50,090
Mr. Ma, please give us a comment.

379
00:29:50,090 --> 00:29:51,090
- How do you feel?
- No comment.

380
00:29:52,250 --> 00:29:54,690
This was absolutely
the expected result.

381
00:29:55,330 --> 00:29:58,930
I'm glad the judge
made a just ruling.

382
00:30:00,170 --> 00:30:04,090
I hope this matter
can now be put to rest.

383
00:30:04,450 --> 00:30:05,570
So what happens now?

384
00:30:05,570 --> 00:30:06,770
They can claim the body,

385
00:30:06,850 --> 00:30:08,090
and I can't do anything?

386
00:30:15,690 --> 00:30:17,330
Okay, thank you.

387
00:30:32,330 --> 00:30:33,330
Did you check his background?

388
00:30:34,690 --> 00:30:36,130
I'm not as fast as Senior was.

389
00:30:36,730 --> 00:30:37,930
Then work harder to make up for it.

390
00:30:38,250 --> 00:30:39,250
Why are you still standing here?

391
00:30:59,190 --> 00:31:01,950
There's no helping it if the law
can't keep up with the times.

392
00:31:03,350 --> 00:31:06,070
I'll find a way
to make that jerk compromise.

393
00:31:13,110 --> 00:31:15,270
My wife said she won't divorce me.

394
00:31:18,030 --> 00:31:19,670
She's supporting me in quitting.

395
00:31:25,790 --> 00:31:27,070
Have you decided?

396
00:31:38,150 --> 00:31:39,150
That's good.

397
00:31:44,630 --> 00:31:45,630
No change.

398
00:31:47,110 --> 00:31:48,110
Business as usual.

399
00:31:52,390 --> 00:31:54,670
Yes, no change is good.

400
00:31:56,470 --> 00:31:57,750
Do you really think so?

401
00:32:35,830 --> 00:32:36,830
Time to get off work.

402
00:32:37,430 --> 00:32:38,430
So soon?

403
00:32:38,950 --> 00:32:41,990
Closing early
for New Year's Eve dinner.

404
00:32:50,110 --> 00:32:52,070
- Where are you going?
- Next door, to keep working.

405
00:32:53,390 --> 00:32:56,030
I mean, let's get off work together
and have a reunion dinner.

406
00:32:58,430 --> 00:32:59,550
You don't have to pity me.

407
00:33:01,350 --> 00:33:02,590
It's you who should pity me.

408
00:33:09,350 --> 00:33:11,750
Homemade food. A taste of home.

409
00:33:32,670 --> 00:33:33,870
How is it? Is it okay?

410
00:33:38,470 --> 00:33:39,470
Yes.

411
00:33:44,470 --> 00:33:45,950
- Hello.
- Dad.

412
00:33:46,030 --> 00:33:48,670
We ate a lot of sushi
at Tsukiji today.

413
00:33:48,830 --> 00:33:51,350
So much of it. Have you eaten?

414
00:33:51,830 --> 00:33:53,510
I'm eating now.
Look how much I have.

415
00:33:54,110 --> 00:33:55,230
What's that dish?

416
00:33:55,910 --> 00:33:57,590
- This one?
- The one next to it.

417
00:33:58,030 --> 00:33:59,350
This dish is chicken.

418
00:34:00,990 --> 00:34:02,030
How are you doing?

419
00:34:02,110 --> 00:34:05,270
I went to Ginza today
and bought this suit for you.

420
00:35:05,830 --> 00:35:06,830
Winning hand!

421
00:35:06,830 --> 00:35:08,670
Winning on the last tile!

422
00:35:09,870 --> 00:35:11,790
Self-draw,
all one suit, all triplets.

423
00:35:11,870 --> 00:35:13,390
Double East,
fully concealed hand.

424
00:35:13,470 --> 00:35:15,230
I won big!

425
00:35:15,550 --> 00:35:16,550
Pay me.

426
00:35:16,550 --> 00:35:18,030
How many points?

427
00:35:19,790 --> 00:35:20,870
You again?

428
00:35:21,910 --> 00:35:23,270
Are you cheating?

429
00:35:24,950 --> 00:35:26,550
You had better not
be playing tricks.

430
00:35:28,310 --> 00:35:29,830
Is this how you act when you lose?

431
00:35:29,910 --> 00:35:32,190
Buddy, show some sportsmanship.

432
00:35:32,910 --> 00:35:36,230
Just pay him. You have
to spend money to make money.

433
00:35:50,550 --> 00:35:51,550
Hi.

434
00:35:54,190 --> 00:35:56,590
Thank you for looking after me
all these years.

435
00:36:00,350 --> 00:36:03,110
I've liked you
since I studied history as a kid.

436
00:36:05,710 --> 00:36:08,510
You really have
a divine aura in person.

437
00:36:11,510 --> 00:36:12,590
I need to talk to you.

438
00:36:15,150 --> 00:36:18,310
It's fine. Carry on.

439
00:36:21,590 --> 00:36:22,590
Let's talk outside.

440
00:36:25,510 --> 00:36:27,550
Were those real deities
or just cosplayers?

441
00:36:27,790 --> 00:36:28,910
I thought I could only see ghosts...

442
00:36:28,990 --> 00:36:29,990
Shut up!

443
00:36:32,310 --> 00:36:33,430
What's wrong with you?

444
00:36:33,710 --> 00:36:34,910
Trespassing in a divine abode
is one thing.

445
00:36:34,990 --> 00:36:36,150
But you should've pretended not
to see them.

446
00:36:36,230 --> 00:36:37,390
Even if you really could see them,

447
00:36:37,470 --> 00:36:38,870
don't say you're here for me.

448
00:36:39,270 --> 00:36:41,030
Now they know about us.

449
00:36:43,670 --> 00:36:45,990
You've really done me in this time.

450
00:36:46,230 --> 00:36:48,110
What? What do you mean?

451
00:36:48,430 --> 00:36:50,150
Letting you return to the living
was a special case.

452
00:36:50,230 --> 00:36:51,230
It's against the rules.

453
00:36:51,310 --> 00:36:52,630
No one is supposed to know.

454
00:36:52,710 --> 00:36:55,350
Now you just waltz in here
asking for me.

455
00:36:57,550 --> 00:37:00,070
Even a 20,000-word report
won't cut it.

456
00:37:01,470 --> 00:37:03,190
If you hadn't tricked me,
would I have needed to find you?

457
00:37:03,790 --> 00:37:04,790
What are you talking about?

458
00:37:05,230 --> 00:37:06,470
I've done so many good deeds
to help people.

459
00:37:06,550 --> 00:37:07,950
Why did the line get longer instead?

460
00:37:10,830 --> 00:37:14,190
Is wanting an affair
considered immoral?

461
00:37:16,990 --> 00:37:18,270
I was just thinking about it.

462
00:37:18,710 --> 00:37:19,910
Can't I even think about it?

463
00:37:20,710 --> 00:37:22,630
I really like him.
I can't control myself.

464
00:37:22,710 --> 00:37:24,670
You're after someone else's husband
and you're acting so righteous?

465
00:37:24,750 --> 00:37:25,750
I don't want to waste my breath.

466
00:37:25,790 --> 00:37:27,470
It's purely platonic.

467
00:37:27,990 --> 00:37:29,550
Plus, I've continued
to do good deeds to help others.

468
00:37:29,550 --> 00:37:31,350
Why didn't it cancel out?
Why did the line get longer?

469
00:37:31,630 --> 00:37:33,190
Being a person is
like being a goalkeeper.

470
00:37:33,270 --> 00:37:36,390
No matter how many saves you make,
if you concede one, you lose.

471
00:37:36,470 --> 00:37:38,790
It takes a lot of work
to win it back after that.

472
00:37:38,870 --> 00:37:40,710
It's not an equal trade.

473
00:37:49,710 --> 00:37:51,350
Get out. Now.

474
00:38:07,910 --> 00:38:10,590
Why can this young lady see us?

475
00:38:12,110 --> 00:38:13,190
She's dying.

476
00:38:13,990 --> 00:38:16,630
Dying means she's not dead yet.

477
00:38:16,910 --> 00:38:17,990
Why does she know you?

478
00:38:19,430 --> 00:38:20,510
That's my secret.

479
00:38:21,150 --> 00:38:22,910
Don't be so nosy.
Let's start the next round.

480
00:38:22,990 --> 00:38:24,910
Come on. Start the next round.

481
00:38:25,070 --> 00:38:26,550
Can we not count that last round?

482
00:38:26,630 --> 00:38:27,750
Of course.

483
00:38:41,470 --> 00:38:42,470
You said you would help me.

484
00:38:44,270 --> 00:38:45,470
I'm handling it.

485
00:38:45,790 --> 00:38:47,070
They're cremating me
the day after tomorrow.

486
00:38:47,150 --> 00:38:48,710
Then they'll put me
in their ancestral hall.

487
00:38:48,790 --> 00:38:50,070
I won't be able
to go back to Australia.

488
00:38:51,350 --> 00:38:52,350
I don't understand!

489
00:38:52,430 --> 00:38:53,670
Cathy and I are already married.

490
00:38:53,750 --> 00:38:55,190
Why do I still have
to be bullied by them?

491
00:38:55,710 --> 00:38:56,870
If the legal process doesn't work,

492
00:38:56,950 --> 00:38:58,190
I'll definitely find a way
to help you.

493
00:38:58,590 --> 00:38:59,830
You won't find any dirt on him.

494
00:39:00,110 --> 00:39:01,270
I will. Trust me.

495
00:39:01,350 --> 00:39:03,390
I'm his daughter.
I know what kind of person he is.

496
00:39:03,470 --> 00:39:05,110
He's very careful in everything.
You won't find anything.

497
00:39:07,230 --> 00:39:08,310
I have another way.

498
00:39:09,070 --> 00:39:10,070
Visit him in a dream.

499
00:39:10,630 --> 00:39:12,470
Tell him your final wishes yourself.

500
00:39:14,030 --> 00:39:15,950
He never really listened to me
when I was alive.

501
00:39:16,270 --> 00:39:17,470
Let alone now that I'm dead.

502
00:39:18,350 --> 00:39:19,470
That's how people are.

503
00:39:19,790 --> 00:39:21,950
They never have anything nice to say
while they're alive.

504
00:39:22,350 --> 00:39:24,270
They only see the good
in each other after death.

505
00:39:25,470 --> 00:39:26,470
You are his daughter.

506
00:39:26,670 --> 00:39:28,270
No matter how much you clashed
when you were alive,

507
00:39:28,350 --> 00:39:29,550
he will still listen to you.

508
00:39:31,390 --> 00:39:33,910
Sometimes, families just need
a chance to be honest.

509
00:39:34,910 --> 00:39:36,190
Just give it a try first.

510
00:39:36,470 --> 00:39:38,750
If it doesn't work,
I'll think of another way.

511
00:39:39,430 --> 00:39:41,110
Remember, stay calm.

512
00:39:45,750 --> 00:39:47,030
I'll trust you one more time.
